alejandra: opening a tiny PR: private/VPC migration mini-notes. includes MTU tips, minimal PKCS#11 example, sha256 checksum for air-gapped bundles, compact installer vs runtime ports, and a short JS proxy snippet. need one reviewer.

mike: please clearly mark installer-only vs runtime ports. keep the list short.

jin: replacement HSM link: https://hsm-vendor.example.com/linux-pkcs11-guide. pkcs11 example to include:

pkcs11_library=/usr/lib/libpkcs11.so
slot_label=redwood-hsm-slot

emily: checksum snippet (sha256) looks good. i'll validate on sealed-site-qa1 once PR is up. add dos2unix note for windows transfers.

alejandra: JS proxy snippet (avoid rejectUnauthorized):
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
const HttpsProxyAgent = require('https-proxy-agent');
const agent = new HttpsProxyAgent('http://proxy.local:3128');
await fetch('https://redwood.internal/api/v1/generate', { method: 'POST', agent, headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_KEY}` }, body: JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'hi' }) });

